WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:14.384
months passed quickly.

2
00:00:15.225 --> 00:00:18.886
Lightfoot, our wild donkey, produced a foal that we named Swift.

3
00:00:19.547 --> 00:00:21.687
We built a porch across the front of Rockburg.

4
00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:27.550
Aside from those events, all was quiet until Jack had a misadventure one afternoon.

5
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.772
He often went off by himself and came back with new things to show us.

6
00:00:32.876 --> 00:00:36.660
But this time he reappeared covered with mud and almost in tears.

7
00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.141
"What happened?"

8
00:00:38.401 --> 00:00:38.721
I said.

9
00:00:38.741 --> 00:00:39.863
"Where have you been?"

10
00:00:39.883 --> 00:00:44.747
"I went to get reeds to make baskets, and I fell into the swamp.

11
00:00:45.528 --> 00:00:47.149
I called and called for help.

12
00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.052
But nobody came and I kept sinking."

13
00:00:50.953 --> 00:00:54.115
He had finally managed to cut some reeds and fasten them into a bundle.

14
00:00:54.976 --> 00:00:58.840
Meanwhile Fangs, his jackal, had run back and forth at the edge of the swamp.

15
00:00:59.604 --> 00:01:03.067
"I used the reeds like a raft to keep from sinking," said Jack.

16
00:01:03.087 --> 00:01:07.470
"When I finally freed my legs from the swamp, I caught hold of Fangs.

17
00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.411
He pulled me to dry land!"

18
00:01:09.431 --> 00:01:12.874
"Fangs is truly a hero," I said.

19
00:01:12.894 --> 00:01:15.916
"But next time take one of your brothers along."

20
00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:22.701
We wanted to make baskets because we needed something for gathering and storing fruits and root vegetables.

21
00:01:23.721 --> 00:01:27.124
After some trial and effort, we produced a good supply of baskets.

22
00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.922
One basket was especially large.

23
00:01:30.743 --> 00:01:35.507
While weaving it, I left holes so that a strong stick could be passed through the holes.

24
00:01:36.428 --> 00:01:39.851
In that way two people could carry the basket when it was full and heavy.

25
00:01:39.871 --> 00:01:41.813
"Do you see how this will work?"

26
00:01:42.093 --> 00:01:42.854
I asked the boys.

27
00:01:42.874 --> 00:01:44.395
"Oh, yes!"

28
00:01:44.716 --> 00:01:46.097
Jack's eyes lit up with fun.

29
00:01:46.938 --> 00:01:50.101
He and Ernest ran a sturdy piece of bamboo through the holes.

30
00:01:50.961 --> 00:01:53.424
Then Fritz popped little Franz into the basket.

31
00:01:54.164 --> 00:01:57.985
The boys took turns carrying Franz around while he whooped with delight.

32
00:01:58.845 --> 00:01:59.425
"Oh, Father!"

33
00:01:59.666 --> 00:02:00.206
cried Fritz.

34
00:02:00.226 --> 00:02:02.786
"Don't you think we could make something like this for Mother?

35
00:02:03.527 --> 00:02:06.807
It would be more comfortable for her than jolting along in our cart."

36
00:02:07.548 --> 00:02:09.628
The boys shouted with glee at the proposal.

37
00:02:09.648 --> 00:02:11.329
"What do you think, Mother?"

38
00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:12.289
asked Ernest.

39
00:02:12.309 --> 00:02:17.830
"Well, I think you could make it, but She hesitated.

40
00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:23.512
"I'm not sure I'd like sitting in the middle of a big basket, peering over the rim."

41
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:28.101
"We wouldn't make you sit on the bottom of a basket."

42
00:02:28.382 --> 00:02:28.882
I laughed.

43
00:02:29.542 --> 00:02:30.963
"We'd make you a comfortable seat."

44
00:02:31.803 --> 00:02:35.084
"It would be a bit like a sedan chair," explained Ernest.

45
00:02:35.104 --> 00:02:37.465
"I've seen pictures of those in books."

46
00:02:37.485 --> 00:02:41.487
"Yes," I replied, "but who would carry this chair?"

47
00:02:42.448 --> 00:02:46.509
I worried that the boys would grow tired or stumble, and then the chair would fall.

48
00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:48.810
"The bull and the buffalo!"

49
00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:49.731
cried Jack.

50
00:02:50.471 --> 00:02:51.331
"Why not use them?

51
00:02:51.811 --> 00:02:52.692
Let's try them now!"

52
00:02:53.688 --> 00:02:58.771
Off ran the boys, and in a short time the basket was securely hung between the two animals.

53
00:02:59.691 --> 00:03:05.174
Fritz and Jack sprang into their saddles, and Ernest very carefully deposited himself in the basket.

54
00:03:05.895 --> 00:03:07.956
They set forth at a slow, steady pace.

55
00:03:08.756 --> 00:03:13.259
The animals, who were quite docile, appeared only a little surprised at their new task.

56
00:03:13.279 --> 00:03:15.560
"Oh, it's so pleasant, Mother!"

57
00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.621
called out Ernest as they passed us.

58
00:03:17.641 --> 00:03:20.483
"The basket rocks as gently as a cradle.

59
00:03:20.863 --> 00:03:22.244
Faster, Fritz, faster!"

60
00:03:22.932 --> 00:03:26.874
Fritz and Jack urged their animals to trot, and Ernest liked that ride too.

61
00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:31.015
But then the pace quickened, making the basket shake violently.

62
00:03:32.116 --> 00:03:32.856
"Stop, Fritz!"

63
00:03:33.156 --> 00:03:33.816
yelled Ernest.

64
00:03:34.557 --> 00:03:35.197
"Halt, Jack!

65
00:03:35.497 --> 00:03:36.117
Stop now!

66
00:03:36.798 --> 00:03:37.738
Can anybody hear me?"

67
00:03:38.598 --> 00:03:41.479
But Fritz and Jack thought it was great fun to shake up their brother.

68
00:03:41.499 --> 00:03:43.920
"What's the matter, professor?"

69
00:03:44.121 --> 00:03:44.741
called Jack.

70
00:03:44.761 --> 00:03:48.562
"Didn't sedan chairs go this fast in those books you read?"

71
00:03:49.683 --> 00:03:52.684
The boys made a circuit of the level ground in front of Rockburg.

72
00:03:53.312 --> 00:03:56.614
They finally pulled up in front of us like performers awaiting applause.

73
00:03:57.395 --> 00:04:00.917
It was hard not to laugh, but Ernest was very angry with them.

74
00:04:01.818 --> 00:04:02.979
"You could have killed me!"

75
00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:04.320
he cried angrily.

76
00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:07.142
"Don't be ridiculous," said Fritz.

77
00:04:07.562 --> 00:04:11.845
"You're acting like—" "Quiet, everyone," I said for I could see an argument building up.

78
00:04:11.865 --> 00:04:15.228
"Taking a joke too far can only lead to bad feelings.

79
00:04:16.048 --> 00:04:19.030
If we're going to survive, we need to keep peace among ourselves."

80
00:04:19.871 --> 00:04:24.078
Fritz and Jack apologized, and Ernest helped them to unharness the bull and buffalo.

81
00:04:25.539 --> 00:04:29.542
Then Fritz joined my wife and me on the front porch while the other boys played below.

82
00:04:30.342 --> 00:04:34.325
We were chatting pleasantly when Fritz suddenly stood up and stared off into the distance.

83
00:04:35.266 --> 00:04:37.827
"Something strange is coming toward the bridge," he said.

84
00:04:37.847 --> 00:04:41.010
"First it was coiled up on the ground like a hose.

85
00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.571
Now it's rising up and sinking back again."

86
00:04:43.591 --> 00:04:46.934
"Take the other boys inside at once," I told my wife.

87
00:04:46.954 --> 00:04:49.576
"Close the door."

88
00:04:50.912 --> 00:04:54.419
Fritz stayed by my side while I examined the object through my telescope.

89
00:04:54.439 --> 00:04:58.286
"It's just as I feared," I said, laying down the telescope.

90
00:04:58.306 --> 00:05:00.911
"A giant snake is advancing toward us!"
